<section id="1001I_S000I" variety="S000I">
<name>Door Lock</name>
<ttl id="1001I_S000I_744CK_T004G" variety="T004G">
<name>Power Door Lock System</name>
<para id="RM000000R8E006X" category="J" type-id="302R2" name-id="622PY-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Only rear LH door cannot be locked or unlocked</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000R8E006X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000028000000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>When the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) receives a door lock/unlock request signal, it drives the door lock motor of each seat to lock/unlock all doors.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The power door lock system uses large-scale body multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" to perform the "communication function inspection" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000R8E006X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000028100000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B156937J04" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000R8E006X_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000R8E006X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000R8E006X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000028300000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Rear Door Lock Assembly LH - Main Body ECU (Instrument Panel Junction Block Assembly))</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the rear door lock assembly LH connector and connector A of the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B159248J04" width="2.775699831in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002004006X"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="1" colname="C01" colwidth="2.26in"/>
<colspec colnum="2" colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="0.95in"/>
<colspec colnum="3" colname="C02" colwidth="0.92in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Door Lock - Main Body ECU)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1(UL) - A4(ACT-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4(L) - A3(ACT+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000R8E006X_04_0001" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000R8E006X_04_0005" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000R8E006X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000028200000">
<testtitle>Inspect Rear Door Lock Assembly LH</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Door Lock Operation Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B124017J03" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Inspect the door lock operation when battery voltage is applied to each terminal of the connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="1" colname="C01" colwidth="2.73in"/>
<colspec colnum="2" colname="C02" colwidth="1.4in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Battery connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Door Lock Operation</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Battery positive → 4 (L)</ptxt>
<ptxt>Battery negative → 1 (UL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>LOCK</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Battery positive → 1 (UL)</ptxt>
<ptxt>Battery negative → 4 (L)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>UNLOCK</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000R8E006X_04_0003" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000R8E006X_04_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
